    affiliation: "Department of Viticulture and Enology, University of California, Davis"
repository-code: "https://github.com/prem-p-singh/RNASeq-pipeline"
url: "https://github.com/prem-p-singh/RNASeq-pipeline"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - RNA-seq
  - differential expression
  - Snakemake
  - reproducible research
  - bioinformatics workflow
abstract: >-
  An Excel- and configuration-driven Snakemake workflow for annotated non-UMI
  bulk RNA-seq on Linux x86_64, locally or on SLURM clusters. Canonical sample,
  library and read records support checked within-library lane merging.
  Species, experimental design and
  downstream analyses are set in configuration rather than in code. Study design
  is validated for estimability before compute is committed, unsupported
  assay, design and backend combinations are rejected at preflight, and each
  analysis reports an explicit status so that an empty result is distinguishable
  from a failed or omitted one.
